\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Two nests with nearly the same composition (yellow and orange; Simpson heterogeneity 0.54{} and 0.51). Top: photos. Bottom: mixing index and cell entropy at increasing distances, with the median and interquartile range of all photos. In 107 the colours form large patches ($M(12\,\text  {mm}) = 0.38$); in 302 the orange strands are scattered through the yellow ($M(12\,\text  {mm}) = 0.86$).}}{5}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mixing}{{3}{5}{Two nests with nearly the same composition (yellow and orange; Simpson heterogeneity \exAhet {} and \exBhet ). Top: photos. Bottom: mixing index and cell entropy at increasing distances, with the median and interquartile range of all photos. In 107 the colours form large patches ($M(12\,\text {mm}) = \exAmix $); in 302 the orange strands are scattered through the yellow ($M(12\,\text {mm}) = \exBmix $)}{figure.caption.15}{}}
